{"name":"Romantic Vampire","hex":"#991166","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"romantic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a work of literature, a writer etc.: being like or having the characteristics of a romance, or poetic tale of a mythic or quasi-historical time; fantastic. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Fictitious, imaginary."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person with romantic character (a character like those of the knights in a mythic romance).","A person who is behaving romantically (in a manner befitting someone who feels an idealized form of love)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/romantic"},{"term":"vampire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythological creature (usually humanoid and undead) said to feed on the blood or life energy of the living. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A person with habits traditionally ascribed to (literal) vampires, such as heliophobia, being a night owl, having pale skin, and so on."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To drain of energy or resources."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vampire"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vampire","blocks":[{"text":"A vampire is a mythical creature with a human-like appearance that subsists by feeding on the vital essence of humans. In European folklore, vampires are undead humanoid creatures that visit loved ones and cause mischief or deaths in the neighbourhoods they inhabited while they were alive. They wear shrouds and are often described as bloated and of ruddy or dark countenance, contrasting with the modern gaunt, pale vampire which dates from the early 19th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Philip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg/330px-Philip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikime